# INTERFACE: Module
# Source of truth : ../data-template.json -> "moduleSchema"
# Live reference  : ../fleet_and_weapons.json -> "modules"
# Generated by    : ../tools/generate_modules.py -- deterministic, no RNG. Re-running
#                   reproduces the catalogue byte-for-byte, so edit the tables in that
#                   script, never the generated files. ../tools/verify_modules.py checks
#                   the invariants below.
# Usage           : one JSON file per module under Modules/<slotType>/<functionClass>/;
#                   Modules/index.json lists every module with its path. A ship references
#                   one by moduleId from moduleSlots.list[].moduleEquipped (see ship.interface)
#
# EXTENSIONS BEYOND data-template.json (marked [+] below)
#   effects        - replaces the single `effect` object. A CIC tower changes accuracy,
#                    initiative and detection at once; one effect could not express that.
#   functionClass  - major | support | specific (see below)
#   slotType       - carried on the module so a fit can be checked against the hull.
#                    Enum extended with `command` and `hangar`; see ship.interface.
#   size           - the slot size the module needs, mirroring weapons and hardpoints
#   mass           - tons, counts against the hull's mass budget
#   mark           - 1 | 2 | 3, matching ship tiers 1 | 2 | 3
#   crewRequired   - crew drawn from the hull's complement
#   hullAffinity   - which shipClass values a `specific` module belongs on; empty for
#                    `major` and `support`, which any hull may fit
#
# FUNCTION CLASS -- what role the module plays on the ship
#   major     a core system a warship is built around: propulsion, power generation,
#             command, primary sensors. Any hull may fit one.
#   support   a force multiplier that amplifies or sustains other systems: repair,
#             ECM, shield boosters, armour. Any hull may fit one.
#   specific  mission equipment only certain hull types carry -- minesweep gear, seaplane
#             catapult, cargo derrick, landing craft davits. Constrained by hullAffinity.
#
# INVARIANTS (enforced by tools/verify_modules.py)
#   - moduleIds and names unique; field set identical to the schema below
#   - every effect targets a stat in the vocabulary; no invented stat names
#   - mark ladders monotonic: benefits non-decreasing, drawbacks non-increasing,
#     Mk.3 effect set a superset of Mk.1's
#   - functionClass 'specific' has a non-empty hullAffinity; 'major'/'support' empty
#   - every hullAffinity entry is a real shipClass value
#   - folder placement matches slotType/functionClass
#   - every moduleEquipped reference in fleet_and_weapons.json -> ships still resolves
#
# <<< generated from tools/generate_modules.py -- do not edit by hand
# ARCHETYPES -- 45 module lines, each built at Mk.1 / Mk.2 / Mk.3.
#   Mk.N is meant for a tier-N hull: benefits scale x1.20 per mark, drawbacks
#   shrink x0.90, power and crew rise more slowly, and Mk.3 adds a second effect
#   where the archetype has one.
#
#   archetype              slot       class     size      pwr crew   mass  effects at Mk.1
